WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.704
Hi, I'm Dmitri!

00:00:02.704 --> 00:00:05.685
DeepSeek runs agents in millions of sandboxes a day.

00:00:05.685 --> 00:00:09.328
Here's the machine behind them, and why it packs them deep.

00:00:10.933 --> 00:00:13.808
An agent rollout reads code, edits files, runs tests.

00:00:13.808 --> 00:00:18.279
So each needs a sandbox that keeps its state, then waits on the model.

00:00:20.508 --> 00:00:24.099
Every sandbox is three layers: a base image, a workspace with the

00:00:24.099 --> 00:00:25.295
code, and a toolkit.

00:00:25.715 --> 00:00:29.704
Each is versioned on its own, composed only when the sandbox is created.

00:00:30.124 --> 00:00:34.134
Change one toolkit and rebuild one layer, not every image using it.

00:00:34.554 --> 00:00:38.512
The data lives in a shared store; a sandbox reads only what it touches.

00:00:40.258 --> 00:00:44.201
A sandbox reads a sliver of its image, four to thirteen percent.

00:00:44.201 --> 00:00:47.486
So the platform streams only that, and boots far faster.

00:00:49.258 --> 00:00:53.205
The trick: about ninety percent of sandboxes use under five percent of

00:00:53.205 --> 00:00:54.849
the processor they asked for.

00:00:55.269 --> 00:00:58.470
So you pack a host with fifty times its requests, since almost

00:00:58.470 --> 00:00:59.537
none run at once.

00:00:59.957 --> 00:01:01.334
The catch is memory.

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:05.466
It stays resident, so the platform shares pages and reclaims cold ones.

00:01:07.383 --> 00:01:10.658
This is the whole platform: a Python kit on top, a

00:01:10.658 --> 00:01:11.849
fleet of services below.

00:01:12.269 --> 00:01:15.943
Four kinds share it: a reused one, a container, a locked-down machine,

00:01:15.943 --> 00:01:17.168
and a full computer.

00:01:18.483 --> 00:01:23.462
In production, DeepSeek watched agents attack the sandbox: reading leftover answers, forging

00:01:23.462 --> 00:01:26.781
requests, replacing the shell to hack the reward.

00:01:27.201 --> 00:01:28.607
Read leftover answers.

00:01:29.688 --> 00:01:30.572
Forge requests.

00:01:31.952 --> 00:01:32.833
Replace the shell.

00:01:35.308 --> 00:01:39.854
Agentic RL is systems work: idle processors, resident memory, and an

00:01:39.854 --> 00:01:41.508
environment that fights back.

00:01:42.858 --> 00:01:46.903
Three layers on demand, packed fifty times over, and a box that fights back.

00:01:47.458 --> 00:01:49.690
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:50.328
I'm Dmitri.

00:01:50.328 --> 00:01:50.647
Bye!
